Version 0.3.0:
    * Architecture following ARCHI.md:
      - compact robot API: Robot/RobotSession, SoA JointSet in SI units,
        sensors, actuators and RobotBackend (MuJoCo, kinematic, hardware)
      - every sensor and actuator is a resource; failures make it unavailable
      - SkillScheduler: resources, priorities, preemption, cancellation,
        preconditions and trace; behavior tree actions request skills
      - perception: Camera/FrameSource, PerceptionPipeline of Detectors,
        WorldModel with gating, landmark localization
      - seed hierarchy: replayable worlds, faults and sensor noise
      - scenario YAML: sensors, actuators, randomized objects, faults
      - EnvironmentPool for parallel and deterministic reinforcement learning
      - no OpenCV nor rendering in the library (SceneView hooks)
    * Simulator: rendered wrist camera, color detector, resources/faults
      panel, skill timeline with reasons, emergency stop, seed replay
    * Demos: LineFollower (AprilTag localization, OpenCV line tracking) and
      PickAndPlaceRL

Version 0.2.0:
    * Initial refactor:
      - using personal OpenGL renderer as third party managing USRD/STL and kinematic chain
      - using personal behavior tree as third party
      - using Pinnochio and Mujoco as third parties for IK and phyical engine
      - using behavior tree and robot skills
      - introduce scenario file: constructing the world and assertions on robot/world states
      - Standalone with pick and place demo using camera attached to the robot
      - not integrated: teach pendant and trajectory, behavior tree editor
      - evolution: compact display of behavior tree with color and timelines of skills

Version 0.1.0:
    * Initial commit
    * Functional but naive librarie:
      - home made OpenGL rendering
      - home made kinematic chain
      - home made inverse kinematic
      - URDF/STL loader
      - behavior tree and Prolog integrated but not used
    * Functional standalone application:
      - dear imgui, displayed robot, teach pendant, trajectory ...